{title: God Intended It for Good}
{subtitle: Genesis 45:1–15; 50:15–21}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 82}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [–] | [Eb] | [Cm] | [Ab] |
| [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The fa[Eb]mine came to Canaan and the fields [Bb/D]were cracked and bare
Old Ja[Cm]cob sent his sons to Egypt, there was grain [Ab]for buying there
They bowed be[Eb]fore the governor, they did [Bb/D]not know his face
The broth[Cm]er that they sold away was stan[Ab]ding in that place
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
He could not hold it [Eb]any longer, so he [Bb/D]cleared the room
And wept so [Cm]loud that all of Pharaoh's household [Ab]heard it too
I am Joseph, your [Eb]brother, whom you sold in[Bb/D]to Egypt
Come closer [Ab]to me
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]You intended e[Cm]vil against me
But God intended it [Ab]for good
To accomplish what is now [Eb]being done
The saving of many lives
So [Cm]do not be afraid
I will [Ab]provide for you [Eb]and your children
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Do not be distressed, [Bb]and do not be [Eb]angry with yourselves that you sold me [Bb/D]here
God sent me a[Cm]head of you to preserve life
It was not you [Ab]who sent me here, but God
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
The [Eb]years went by and Jacob died, the [Bb/D]brothers shook with fear
What [Cm]if he holds a grudge against us, now [Ab]our father is not here
[Cm]They fell down at his feet and said, we are [Ab]your slaves today
But Joseph wept and [Eb]spoke to them, and kindly he would say
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
You in[Cm]tended evil against me
[Ab]But God intend[Eb]ed it for good
To accomplish what [Bb]is now being done
The [Ab]saving of many lives
So [Bb]do not be afraid
I will provide for you and your children
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
But God intended it for good
The saving of many lives
{end_of_verse}

